The JSON parse errors are swallowed.

lib/WWW/Crawl4AI/Client.pm:332 decodes the body inside an eval, but never looks at $@. On a 200 with an HTML body $data stays undef, and the parsers answer quietly wrong: parse_crawl_response gives [] (:349), parse_md_response gives undef (:370), parse_job_status_response gives {status => 'UNKNOWN'} (:386), parse_health_response gives 1 (:409).

Failure case: the login page of a captive portal or of a proxy answers the health request with 200 and HTML. health() reports "ok", www-crawl4ai-doctor prints "ok", and the strategy chain reports "all crawl strategies failed (no_strategies)" instead of "the answer was no JSON".

Decide: the decode is checked and WWW::Crawl4AI::Error (type api, with status, method and path) is raised.

The test that holds this down must be red against the old lib/ and fail as a failed expectation, not as a die.

Commit e1b7d59: _decode checks the decode result, a non-empty body that is no JSON raises a type=api error with status, method and path; an empty body stays allowed and is not decoded. Decision (within the card): parse_health_response answers 1 for a JSON object and 0 for every other answer - a JSON scalar (false, true, number, string), a JSON array and an empty body; healthy is only claimed when an object arrives, and an empty body stays error-free per the house rule. Suite: 15 files / 119 tests green (offline).

